;; Standoff argument map for draft8.tex.
;;
;; Each unit of the paper is tagged with the thesis points from intro.edn that it
;; serves, and given a verdict from ONE test:
;;
;;     :counterfactual -- name the conclusion that fails if this unit is removed.
;;
;; A unit with no such conclusion is not "bad"; it is not part of THIS argument.
;; That distinction is the whole point of the map (cf. mmca/verified-but-idle-link).
;;
;; Verdicts:
;;   :load-bearing  a stated conclusion fails without it
;;   :supporting    no conclusion fails, but it supplies definitions or scope a
;;                  load-bearing unit needs
;;   :compress      the conclusion it serves needs far less than it currently spends
;;   :relocate      sound work, serving an argument this paper does not make
;;   :cut           neither serves the argument nor is referenced

{:thesis-source "intro.edn"

 :points [:object :parameter-reading :dynamical-reading :currency
          :endogenous :from-inside :scope :roadmap]

 :units
 [;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- Part I
  {:id :sec/example-2015 :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "The 2015 Example"
   :serves [:object]
   :claim "The originating example is a non-bijective writing outside the permutation core."
   :counterfactual "None. The intro's :object point already states this, and fig:fig2pair
                    is what the reader needs."
   :verdict :compress
   :note "A section for provenance. The figure earns its place; the surrounding
          narrative is told twice."}

  {:id :sec/object :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "The Object"
   :serves [:object]
   :claim "Definition of the two-layer substrate, displayed-position indexing, and
           Equation (1) defining P_sigma."
   :counterfactual "Everything. Equation (1) is referenced throughout, including by
                    Part III's exotype transition."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sec/classification :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "The Classification"
   :serves [:parameter-reading]
   :claim "Fixed rules exist iff every cycle of sigma is even; an all-even sigma with k
           cycles has 2^k of them."
   :counterfactual "The lambda=1/2 result has no domain to quantify over. :parameter-reading
                    fails."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sec/balance :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "Every Fixed Point Is Balanced"
   :serves [:parameter-reading]
   :claim "Every fixed rule of every operator in the family has lambda = 1/2."
   :counterfactual "The paper's central negative -- that the classical coordinate cannot
                    discriminate -- is unproved. This is the load-bearing theorem of Part I."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sub/dead-genotype :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "A dead genotype can carry a live phenotype"
   :serves [:object :dynamical-reading]
   :claim "Genotype aliveness and phenotype aliveness are separable properties."
   :counterfactual "Part III's persistence criterion would be ambiguous about which layer
                    it measures. Establishes the distinction the whole paper relies on."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sec/census :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "The Census"
   :serves [:parameter-reading]
   :claim "All odd-cycle operators remain genotype-alive; every all-even cycle type
           contains both sustaining and collapsing members."
   :counterfactual "The transition from :parameter-reading to :dynamical-reading loses its
                    ground. The census is what shows that exact fixed-point structure does
                    NOT determine dynamical fate -- odd-cycle operators all live, all-even
                    types split -- which is why a dynamical measurement is needed at all."
   :verdict :load-bearing
   :revised-by "codex-5, 2026-08-07"
   :note "PREVIOUSLY :supporting, on the reasoning that the access thesis does not use the
          parity dichotomy. That was wrong, and inconsistent: :sec/not-attractors makes the
          same algebra-does-not-determine-dynamics point and was marked load-bearing.
          The census is the exhaustive version of it. The defect was in intro.edn, which
          asserts the second reading without grounding the move to it; the repair is to
          the introduction, not to the census. Also not removal-safe: fig:parity is
          referenced from :sec/not-attractors (draft8:736)."}

  {:id :sub/rotate-plus-2 :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "A prospective test: reduced rotate+2"
   :serves []
   :claim "One operator's behaviour under a reduced protocol."
   :counterfactual "Nothing fails formally, but it is the paper's only evidence that a
                    prediction was made BEFORE the check rather than after."
   :verdict :load-bearing
   :revised-by "codex-5, 2026-08-07"
   :note "PREVIOUSLY :compress. 127 words. The space gain is negligible against the
          credibility of showing the test was not wholly retrospective."}

  {:id :sec/not-attractors :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "Fixed Points Are Not Attractors"
   :serves [:parameter-reading]
   :claim "Fixed-point existence does not determine attraction."
   :counterfactual "Without it, lambda=1/2 at the fixed points would suggest the dynamics
                    sit there. Closes the gap between the algebra and the dynamics."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sub/braiding :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "Constructive control by temporal schedules"
   :serves [:dynamical-reading]
   :claim "Alternation sustains diversity; supplies the construction the intro's causal
           measurement is applied to."
   :counterfactual "The intro's :dynamical-reading point cites this construction by name
                    (\\secref{sec:braiding}). Removing it breaks that claim."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sec/metrics-limits :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "Limits of the Tested Distance and Complexity Measures"
   :serves [:scope]
   :claim "The tested distance and complexity measures do not separate the regimes."
   :counterfactual "The move to a causal measure would look unmotivated."
   :verdict :supporting}

  {:id :sec/parameter-test :part "The Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "A Parameter-Space Test"
   :serves [:parameter-reading]
   :claim "The propagator-fraction scan gives a broad crossover, not a critical point."
   :counterfactual "The intro's claim that the parameter-space reading is closed off rests
                    on this plus the balance theorem."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  ;; --------------------------------------------------------------- Part II
  {:id :sec/feedback-construction :part "Beyond the Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "A Feedback-Coupled Construction"
   :serves [:currency]
   :claim "Defines the river construction: a permutation-propagator composed with a
           phenotype-reading step."
   :counterfactual "Nothing in Part II or Part III has an object."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sec/causal :part "Beyond the Permutation Core" :kind :section
   :title "A Causal Measure"
   :serves [:dynamical-reading :currency]
   :claim "Damage reach, calibrated against reference rules; feedback roughly doubles it
           against a matched control."
   :counterfactual "The dynamical reading has no instrument and the doubling claim no
                    ground. Also supplies the calibration Part III's first half uses."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sub/gain :part "Beyond the Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "The coupling as a dial"
   :serves [:currency]
   :claim "Reach is monotone in the gain; the frozen field matches marginals and spatial
           structure so only currency varies."
   :counterfactual "The word 'currency' in the thesis has no referent. THIS IS THE UNIT
                    THAT DEFINES THE PAPER'S COORDINATE."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sub/diversity-axis :part "Beyond the Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "Diversity and conservative transport"
   :serves [:currency]
   :claim "Transport, not sustained diversity, controls reach -- the diversity test."
   :counterfactual "The thesis's 'and no other tested coordinate' clause fails. This is the
                    only unit that RULES OUT a rival coordinate rather than supporting the
                    chosen one."
   :verdict :load-bearing}

  {:id :sub/what-coupling-supplies :part "Beyond the Permutation Core" :kind :subsection
   :title "What the coupling supplies"
   :serves [:currency :scope]
   :claim "Per cell and step, the live phenotype context selects a DIFFERENT rule than a
           frozen context would in 73.1% of cell-steps (76.8% against no context), over
           four seeds. First-match over four candidates puts uninformative re-selection at
           about 75%, so a frozen context carries almost no information about the live
           answer."
   :counterfactual "The currency claim loses its per-step mechanism. This is the only unit
                    establishing that the live read is DETERMINATIVE rather than a
                    tiebreak, and therefore that no phenotype-blind rule could encode a
                    common case in its place."
   :verdict :load-bearing
   :revised-by "claude-14 on review of codex-5, 2026-08-07"
   :note "PREVIOUSLY :compress by us ('nothing; it restates') and :CUT by codex-5. Both
          wrong, and wrong the same way: neither of us read the passage. It is not a
          restatement -- it carries a measurement WITH ITS OWN CHANCE BASELINE (73.1%
          against an uninformative 75%), which is a null comparison found nowhere else in
          the paper. The numbers 73.1 and 76.8 occur only here (verified). Cutting it
          would remove the only per-step evidence that the coupling is not redundant.
          Lesson: a unit that LOOKS like summary prose can carry the argument's only
          null."}

  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------- Part III
  {:id :sec/endogenous-gain :part "Endogenous Coupling and Exotypes" :kind :section
   :title "An Endogenous Gain"
   :serves [:endogenous]
   :claim "A blind gate reproduces the dial exactly; a phenotype-reading gate exceeds it;
           a frozen gate matched in width and statistics does not."
   :counterfactual "The thesis's 'recovers it from a construction that sets the coupling
                    for itself' fails. The frozen-gate control is the load-bearing part."
   :verdict :load-bearing
   :note "Already compressed from three sections to one. The width-gradient analysis
          inside it is the remaining compressible material -- superseded by the frozen
          control, and the paper states the gradient is not decomposed."}

